upstream: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cloudflare/skills/main/skills/wrangler/SKILL.md
verified: 2026-08-16
reason: content is NOT a different generation — it is upstream's exact
  content, split into two files. TASKS.md's characterization is wrong; see
  correction below.
note: Measured 2026-08-16: local SKILL.md 291 lines, upstream SKILL.md 922
  lines — the raw numbers TASKS.md cited are correct. But diffed line 1-281
  of both files: byte-identical. Upstream's remaining lines 282-922 (the KV/
  R2/D1/Vectorize/Hyperdrive/Workers AI/Queues/etc CLI reference) are
  byte-identical to local's references/bindings-cli-reference.md (648
  lines), minus a 7-line header local adds: "Extracted from SKILL.md for
  token economy." So this is a deliberate local restructuring for token
  economy (matching this repo's references/ convention used by other
  skills), not drift and not an older/newer upstream generation.
would_lose_if_wired: _refresh-vendored.sh fetches base/<rel> per local file.
  For SKILL.md that pulls upstream's full 922-line monolith back in,
  destroying the split. For references/bindings-cli-reference.md, base/
  references/bindings-cli-reference.md does not exist upstream (upstream
  has no references/ dir) — refresh reports a fetch failure and leaves that
  file orphaned, stale, and duplicating content now also reinlined into
  SKILL.md.
to_vendor: _refresh-vendored.sh would need to support a file-split (one
  upstream file mapped across N local files) before this can be marked
  vendored; until then, re-splitting after each manual upstream check is a
  human step.
